    <heading>Comparative Experiment Example 5</heading>
    <div class="description-paragraph"> Preparation of Precursor Films!</div>
    <div class="description-paragraph">Precursor film samples were prepared under the following conditions. 31 Kg of powdery polyethylene of high molecular weight (intrinsic viscosity:  η!=16.5 dl/g; bulk density=0.45 g/cm<sup>3</sup>) was placed in a metal mold of 320 mm/100 mm in outer diameter/inner diameter and 350 mm in length, and molding was conducted at a temperature of 200° C. for about 10 hours under pressure, followed by cooling for about 10 hours to obtain an ultra-high molecular weight polyethylene bullet of about the same dimension. Then, this bullet was skived by means of a skive machine to obtain a 100-μ thick skived film. Characteristic properties of the thus obtained film are shown in Table 22.</div>
